  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 1224 PM MDT Sat Jul 25 2026\n\nHOT WITH PM STORMS INTO NEXT WEEK:\n\nHigh pressure has settled in over the Intermountain West and \nremains nearly stationary through much of the week ahead. This \nputs eastern Utah and western Colorado in a west/southwest flow \nregime allowing for plenty of warm air to continue to funnel \nacross the region. As a result, unseasonably warm temperatures \nwith valley highs in the upper 90s, low 100s are here to stay. \nRemain cognizant of the heat and pack an excess of water for \nyour outdoor adventures.\n\nAdditionally, monsoonal moisture continues to slosh around \nunderneath the high. This will support afternoon convection each\nday. Thunderstorms will develop over and favor the high \ncountry, with some showers/storms holding together as they move \noff the terrain and over the valleys. Heavy rainfall will be the\nprimary threat with PWATs over 1\" in place and slow storm \nmotions expected. Please see the hydrology section below for \nmore information. Dew points in the 50s will limit the strength \nof outflow gusts, but gusts up to 45 mph can't be ruled out. \nHail, predominately under half an inch in diameter, rounds out \nthe arsenal of thunderstorm hazards this week.",
